msgstr  "imagemagick"

#: build-src/install/index.md:52
msgid   "libyaz4j (optional)"
msgstr  "libyaz4j (optionnel)"

#: build-src/install/index.md:54
msgid   "The `libyaz4j` dependency is only used by the Z39.50 search queries. "
        "If you don't need the Z39.50 queries you can skip this dependency."
msgstr  "La dependance `libyaz4j` est seulement utilisee par les recherche "
        "Z39.50. Si vous ne comptez pas les utiliser vous pouvez ignorer "
        "celle si."

#: build-src/install/index.md:57
msgid   "Database"
msgstr  "Base de données"

#: build-src/install/index.md:59
msgid   "Now we will create an empty database and a user for numahop. NumaHOP "
        "creates its tables automatically no need to create them yourself. "
        "See the [liquibase chapter](../database/index.md) for more "
        "information."
msgstr  "Maintenant nous allons créer une base de données vide pour NumaHOP. "
        "NumaHOP crée les tables automatiquement donc vous n'avez pas besoin "
        "de les créer vous même. Voir la page sur [liquibase](../database/"
        "index.md) pour plus d'informations."

#: build-src/install/index.md:64
msgid   "Run this suite of commands remplacing the placeholders (`<db-name>`, "
        "`<db-user-name>` and `<db-user-pwd>`) for your setup note these as "
        "you will need to fill them in the config step. You should be greeted "
        "by this command prompt:"
msgstr  "Lancez ces commandes en remplaçant les bouts de texte a substituer "
        "`<db-name>`, `<db-user-name>` et `<db-user-pwd>`. Notez ceux-ci vous "
        "allez en avoir besoin plus tard."

#: build-src/install/index.md:70
msgid   "Let's create the database:"
msgstr  "La commande pour créer la base:"

#: build-src/install/index.md:76
msgid   "Then the user NumaHOP will use to connect to the database:"
msgstr  "Puis créez l'utilisateur que NumaHOP utilisera pour se connecter a "
        "la base de données."

#: build-src/install/index.md:79 build-src/install/index.md:80
msgid   "'<db-user-name>'"
msgstr  ""

#: build-src/install/index.md:80
msgid   "'<db-name>'"
msgstr  ""

#: build-src/install/index.md:83
msgid   "Note these are the minimal rights the user NumaHOP will use needs to "
        "edit the database."
msgstr  "Remarque: Les droits donnés a l'utilisateur sont les droits minimaux "
        "pour que NumaHOP puisse éditer la base de données."

#: build-src/install/index.md:85
msgid   "You can verify that all the information is well defined by running "
        "`SHOW DATABASES;` and `SHOW GRANTS FOR '<db-user-name>'@localhost`. "
        "NumaHOP uses an orm with a migration tool and will automatically "
        "create all the tables it needs for you."
msgstr  "Vous pouvez vérifier que tous est bon en lançant les commandes `SHOW "
        "DATABASES;` et `SHOW GRANTS FOR '<db-user-name>'@localhost`."

#: build-src/install/index.md:88
msgid   "Elastic Search"
msgstr  "Elastic Search"

#: build-src/install/index.md:89
msgid   "Just install elastic search and folow this [documentation](https://"
        "www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/install-"
        "elasticsearch.html \"Elastic Documentation\"). And make sure it is "
        "accessible from where you want to install numahop either by "
        "localhost or an url."
msgstr  "Installez Elastic Search en suivant leur documentation ([lien]"
        "(https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/"
        "install-elasticsearch.html \"Elastic Documentation\"). Et assurez "
        "vous que l'instance Elastic Search soit accessible par localhost ou "
        "une URL."

